  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: out-of-bounds repeat stack access in huge regexps\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-110264.patch: reject patterns whose range\n       repeat or null check IDs overflow in regcomp.c, regerror.c.\n     - CVE-2026-110264\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: wrapped jump offsets in the regexp compiler\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-93577-CVE-2026-97229.patch: check the\n       quantifier expansion size without int overflow and reject programs\n       too big for their offset type in regcomp.c, regint.h, regerror.c.\n     - CVE-2026-93577\n     - CVE-2026-97229\n   * Fix build-time test failures:\n     - debian/patches/exclude-tests-failing-on-build-system.patch: skip the\n       DTrace probe and permission tests, which fail when the test suite runs\n       as root, the TLS tests whose test certificates expired and the\n       Asia/Singapore tests that do not match the installed tzdata",
